{
  "version": 1,
  "questionId": "t10-q01",
  "speechText": "Basically, for large files, I don't process everything inside one API request. I create a background job and process the document step by step. For large documents, I use smaller batches and save the progress, so the job can continue if something fails. In one production issue, a large document caused high memory usage and the OCR job failed. First, I checked the job logs, memory usage, processing time, and which step failed. We found that OCR was both memory-heavy and slow. So we reduced the batch size and concurrency, and added checkpoint and resume. After that, we also moved the heavy OCR inference to a remote GPU service. The OCR time improved from around 46 seconds per page to around 2 seconds per page. So overall, I first make the job recoverable, then measure the bottleneck, and finally optimize the slowest part.",
